course: dictionary
lesson: 13918
title: Leaders: who is in charge or ahead
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A leader is a person who leads, or is in charge of, a group, a team, a country or an organisation. Leaders is the plural, so it means more than one leader. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «The world leaders met in the big hall to talk about peace.» The clues are world and met to talk about peace. These are people in charge of countries, making big decisions.
explain: «The race leaders were already halfway round the track.» Here leaders means the runners or teams in first place. Halfway round the track shows they are ahead of everyone else. Always check by swapping in a simple meaning, such as «the people in charge», and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A leader is a person who leads or is in charge of a group, team, country or organisation.
fact: Leaders is the plural of leader, so it means more than one leader.
fact: «World leaders» means the people in charge of countries around the world.
fact: «The race leaders» means the people or teams in first place.
fact: «Market leaders» means the companies that are the best or most important in their area.
exercise: «The world leaders met in the big hall to talk about peace.» Who are the leaders in this sentence? | The best cooks in town | *People in charge of countries | Dogs in the park | Pupils in the class
exercise: «The race leaders were already halfway round the track.» What does leaders mean here? | *The people or teams in first place | People who sell tickets | Animals that run fast | The last runners
exercise: Which word means more than one leader? | lead | *leaders | leading | leader
test: «Our group leaders check the class list every morning.» What are the group leaders? | The names of the groups | Teachers who ring the bell | Pupils who are always late | *People in charge of each group
test: A company that is one of the best in its area is called a market leader. What does this phrase mean? | Markets where people sell old clothes | Shops that sell only sweets | People who lead the school choir | *Companies that are the best or most important in their area
exam: «Follow the leader» is a game where one child goes first and the others copy. In this game, what does the leader do? | Sleeps under a tree | Hides from the others | *Goes first and shows the others what to do | Counts the points
